_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. The fix is in `pricing/money.py`, and `add_vat` picks it up automatically because it calls `round_money`.\n\n**Why it happened:** the number 2.675 can't be stored exactly as a float. Python actually holds `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so `round()` was right to round it down. Separately, `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. That would break \"half up\" even for inputs that are stored exactly.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the input with `Decimal(repr(x))`. `repr` gives the shortest decimal that maps back to the same float, which is the number the customer typed (`2.675`). It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and still returns a `float`, so callers don't change.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Before the fix, `round` gave `2.67`, `1.0` and `0.12` for 2.675, 1.005 and 0.125.\n- After it, `round_money` gives `2.68`, `1.01` and `0.13`.\n- `add_vat(10)` still returns `12.0`.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering the half-cent cases, a negative value (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`) and a value just below half (`2.674 \u2192 2.67`).\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the new tests and the existing `test_split` by calling them directly with `python3`. All passed. I couldn't confirm the new tests fail without the fix because there's no git checkout to revert to.\n\n`split()` doesn't use `round_money` and I didn't change it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 189202, "requests_cache_write": 74958, "requests_cost_usd": 0.4658304, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2656, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5